==German==

===Etymology===
{{root|de|ine-pro|*sper-}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|sparn}}, from {{inh|de|goh|sparēn}}, {{m|goh|sparōn}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*sparāną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*sper-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ʃpaːɐ̯n/|/ˈʃpaːʁən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-sparen.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[save up]]; to [[accumulate]], to [[put aside]] (for a specific purpose)
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''spare''' mein Geld für ein neues Auto.|I'm '''saving''' my money for a new car.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[save]], to [[conserve]] (for example energy)
#: {{ux|de|Die Heizung herunterdrehen, um Energie zu '''sparen'''.|Turn the heat down to '''save''' energy.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with dative reflexive pronoun and {{m|de|können}}|figuratively}} to be able to save (as unnecessary or useless)
#: {{ux|de|Du kannst dir deinen Atem '''sparen''', er hört nicht auf dich.|You can '''save''' your breath, he's not listening to you.}}
# {{lb|de|ditransitive}} to [[save]], to [[spare]] (from effort, an unpleasant or unnecessary task)
#: {{ux|de|Danke für den Zucker, du '''sparst''' mir einen Besuch im Laden.|Thanks for the sugar, you're '''sparing''' me a visit to the store.}}

